# Publish release

When the user asks to publish a release, complete these steps in order. Stop if any step fails.

1. Update `CHANGELOG.md`: move `[Unreleased]` notes into `## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD`, leave `[Unreleased]` empty, and update the footer compare/tag links. While the major version is 0, compatible additions bump the patch; breaking API or on-disk format changes bump the minor. Set the same version in `package.json`, `src-tauri/Cargo.toml`, and `src-tauri/tauri.conf.json`. Do not rewrite published versions.

2. Follow the before-commit checklist, then commit the release. Do not skip git hooks.

3. Create annotated tag `vX.Y.Z` on that commit:

   ```sh
   git tag -a vX.Y.Z -m "vX.Y.Z"
   ```

4. Push the commit and tag, then publish the GitHub release from the new changelog section:

   ```sh
   git push origin HEAD
   git push origin vX.Y.Z
   gh release create vX.Y.Z --title "vX.Y.Z" --notes "..."
   ```

Do not force-push.
